WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
- Have you ever had anything paranormal

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.320
happen to you in real life?

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.180
- Yeah, in my life,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.400
okay so I'm from South Carolina,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.233
you know, the south,

00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:06.066
and there's a lot of things

00:00:06.066 --> 00:00:07.350
in the south that don't
happen anywhere else,

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.780
you know, there's just
beliefs that they have,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.860
things that they do, rituals.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.350
When I was a kid, I
used to have this thing

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.880
that was sitting on my
chest when I would sleep

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.310
and it was keeping me from getting up

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.020
and I couldn't open my
eyes and I would struggle

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.610
and I couldn't breathe
very well, and I was like,

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.070
this is really, like it's scaring me.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.080
And I would fight and struggle
and I would sit up in my bed,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.240
and I'd look around and it would be

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.090
like someone was holding me down, I swear.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.340
And I'd tell my mom about it.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.860
It would happen night after night.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.150
And as soon as I lay down,

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.360
it would happen again,
it's like holding me

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.800
and I was like, I couldn't open my eyes.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.633
It was scaring me.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:33.466
So we talked about it--

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.299
- What?!

00:00:34.299 --> 00:00:35.132
- Yeah.

00:00:35.132 --> 00:00:36.340
She said it was, it was this thing called,

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.173
it was like a hag.

00:00:37.173 --> 00:00:38.006
It was called a hag.

00:00:38.006 --> 00:00:38.839
And it would ride you

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:39.736
because your spirit was unsettled.

00:00:39.736 --> 00:00:40.569
- Ha!

00:00:40.569 --> 00:00:41.402
Okay.

00:00:41.402 --> 00:00:42.580
(laughing)
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.413
She told me.

00:00:43.413 --> 00:00:44.246
And there was this old woman

00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:45.079
living across the street from me.

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:46.960
And I would talk about her all the time,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.192
because she lived alone,
and she was freaky,

00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:49.250
and she'd never come outside.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.520
So, me and all my cousins
in the neighborhood,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.353
we were afraid of this woman.

00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:54.160
So I think, she's, my mom says,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:54.993
because of your,

00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:55.838
the way you're thinking about this woman

00:00:55.838 --> 00:00:58.029
and she's, her spirit is riding,

00:00:58.029 --> 00:01:00.388
this is the thing that they
do and she had that power.

00:01:00.388 --> 00:01:01.480
That's like a witch!

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.194
- That's creepy and I'm sorry.
- Yeah.

00:01:03.194 --> 00:01:04.501
- I know, I know.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:05.850
I'm still dealing with that right now.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:06.890
I sleep with lights on.
- That would terrify me!

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.820
- Yeah.
- If I couldn't move.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:09.653
- I know.

00:01:09.653 --> 00:01:10.486
I know.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:10.486 --> 00:01:11.680
- Okay, another favorite
thing about you though,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.620
you have a tiny dog, do
you have it to protect you?

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.600
It's a tiny dog.
- No, no, no, no.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.992
- You're just a big man with a tiny dog.

00:01:16.992 --> 00:01:17.825
It's awesome.
(audience screaming)

00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:19.257
It's like, it's funny.

00:01:19.257 --> 00:01:20.770
It's so cute!

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.700
- That, listen that picture says it all.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.510
My dog, listen I didn't
get the dog on my own,

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.100
that wasn't my choice, but
I just feel like, you know,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.796
I don't need a dog to
protect me, I protect my dog.

00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:30.860
That's how I look at it.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.652
My dog is a small dog and I hold my dog.

00:01:32.652 --> 00:01:34.281
And if I see another dog, I pick it up.

00:01:34.281 --> 00:01:35.627
It's, you know,

00:01:35.627 --> 00:01:37.550
(audience clapping)
I'm protecting my dog.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.383
That's how I look at it.

00:01:38.383 --> 00:01:39.216
- Oh my god!

00:01:39.216 --> 00:01:40.798
You think other guys
might be overcompensating?

00:01:40.798 --> 00:01:42.130
- I think they are.
- Like, look at my big dog?

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:42.997
- They got two, they got two pit bulls

00:01:42.997 --> 00:01:43.830
and you're like pulling in the street,

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.663
and you're like yeah, you know, yeah.

00:01:44.663 --> 00:01:45.496
(laughing)

00:01:45.496 --> 00:01:46.900
I'm like, really?

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:47.733
Really?

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:48.566
You have two?

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:49.399
- I love, I love it.

